    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that there isn't \"official\" proof, but that's kind of the point isn't it? if it's a coordinated effort to keep the population docile, they wouldn't just publish papers on it. but if you look at the math behind how 440hz affects resonance compared to 432hz, it's a very specific choice. why do you think the global standard shifted to 440hz specifically? it feels too intentional to be just a coincidence.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
