      "content": "okay but even if it's just \"instrumental consistency,\" why does it feel like it's practically designed to disrupt natural human resonance? it's weird how everything—from music to the electrical grid—seems to be hitting these specific dissonant notes that make it impossible to just feel relaxed or creative. if you look into the way pulse-width modulation works in modern power electronics, wouldn't that kind of subtle frequency interference be the perfect way to disrupt biological rhythms without being obvious? it feels like there's a huge gap between what's \"official\" and what's actually happening to our biology.",
